# Dependencies (to be updated based on chosen framework)
node_modules/
.packages

# 🔴 pubspec.lock IS TRACKED, AND IT IS TRACKED BECAUSE THIS IS AN APPLICATION.
# The Dart team's own rule: libraries leave the lock out, apps commit it. Lupin Mobile is
# an app, and the line that used to sit here ignored it (row 1bc50bf5).
#
# What the ignore cost, measured 2026-09-28: a freshly created worktree has no lock, so
# `pub get` re-resolves EVERY dependency from scratch and picks whatever is newest inside
# the pubspec ranges. That seat drew dio 5.11.1 against the fleet's 5.8.0+1, and dio 5.11.1
# did not compile against this tree — 46 test files failed to load. The merge gate was not
# reproducible on a clean checkout of the exact sha it was gating, which is the one thing a
# gate has to be.
#
# Do not add it back to make a resolution problem go away. If the lock needs to move, move
# it deliberately with `flutter pub upgrade`, run the suite, and commit the new lock as its
# own reviewable change.

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Python virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Local Flutter installation
#
# ⚠️ `/flutter`, NOT `flutter/` — the trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY ONLY, and in a
# provisioned worktree this entry is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's SDK
# (src/scripts/link-worktree-venv.sh). Measured 2026-09-19: under `flutter/` the symlink
# showed as `?? flutter` in every provisioned worktree — untracked, not ignored, and one
# `git add -A` away from committing a machine-specific absolute path into the repo.
/flutter
.flutter/

# Auto-generated Flutter env file (machine-specific paths)
ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh

# Flutter auto-generated build artifacts (machine-specific, regenerated by `flutter pub get`)
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
ios/Runner/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.m

# Claude Code parallel-session manifest (per ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md recommendation)
.claude-session.md

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE workspace files
*.code-workspace
# Session I/O — recordings, captures, analysis plots, scratch artifacts.
# Outputs, not sources: cite the run, don't check the run in. Measured
# 2026-09-22 at 11 MB (wav clips, a git-delta plot, macOS .DS_Store) with
# ZERO files ever tracked — this rule keeps it that way and takes `?? io/`
# out of every `git status`, which is the line read before every commit.
# Rick's call, 2026-09-22: "let's add the entire io/ to gitignore".
io/

# Claude mementos (records + pointers) — NEVER commit: a memento that
# will be committed is written more carefully, and therefore less honestly.
# Kept below the blanket `io/` rule above, which already covers this path:
# it stays for the reason, and so a narrower io/ rule can never lose it.
io/mementos/
.claude-memento.md
.claude-memento-*.md
